    "input": "search_document: Hello! I understand the rules can be confusing, especially when trying to combine different benefits. I will answer your questions strictly based on the Northwind Outdoor handbook excerpts provided.\n\n**1. Can you combine the Student and Military discounts?**\nNo, you cannot combine these discounts to get 20% off. The handbook states that verified students, active-duty military personnel, and first responders are eligible for a **permanent 10% discount** on all regular-priced items [discounts]. It does not state that these discounts are cumulative or stackable. Since both groups receive the same 10% benefit, you would only receive the 10% discount once, regardless of whether you verify as a student, a military member, or both. You must complete the verification process through the third-party partner service to activate this benefit on your account [discounts].\n\n**2. Does the 25% clearance discount apply to all clearance items?**\nThe handbook states that during clearance periods, \"all eligible inventory is marked down by a minimum of 25%\" [discounts]. This means the discount applies to items that are designated as \"eligible inventory\" for the clearance sale. It does not explicitly guarantee that *every single item* in the store is on clearance, but any item marked as part of the clearance sale will have at least a 25% reduction.\n\n**3. Is the 14-day clearance period fixed?**\nYes, the handbook specifies that these clearance periods \"occur for exactly 14 days in January and July\" [discounts]. This indicates the duration is fixed at 14 days for those specific months.\n\n**4. Important Restrictions for Your Purchase**\nSince you plan to buy a bike and camping gear, please note the following critical rules from the handbook:\n\n*   **No Combining Discounts:** Clearance discounts \"cannot be combined with any other promotional codes or loyalty rewards\" [discounts]. This means if you buy an item during the 14-day clearance sale, you **cannot** also apply your 10% student/military discount to that specific item. You must choose which discount applies to each item.\n*   **Bundle Savings:** If you are buying a tent, sleeping bag, and camp stove together, you can get a 15% bundle discount [discounts]. However, this promotion \"does not apply to clearance items\" [discounts]. So, if any of those three items are on clearance, you cannot use the 15% bundle discount.\n*   **Timing:** You must complete your purchase within the 14-day window to secure the reduced price, as items revert to standard retail value immediately after the period ends [discounts].\n\n**Summary for your purchase:**\n*   If you buy **regular-priced** items, you can use your 10% student/military discount [discounts].\n*   If you buy **clearance** items, you get the minimum 25% off, but you **cannot** use your 10% student/military discount on those items [discounts].\n*   You cannot stack the 10% discount with the 25% clearance discount [discounts].\n\nI hope this clarifies the rules for you. If you need further assistance or have questions about specific items, I can offer to escalate the ticket to a human agent.",
